; ============================================================
; TITLE:    String Art Circle
; CATEGORY: Patterns & Mandalas
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     string art, envelope, circle, modular arithmetic, lines
; SUMMARY:  Hammers nails round a circle and winds colored threads from each nail to one further along, layer by layer.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   72 nails stand round a circle. For each layer, a thread runs from
;   every nail to the nail SKIP places further round. Although every
;   thread is straight, together they outline a perfect circle in the
;   middle (an "envelope"). Each layer has its own skip and color, so
;   you get rings inside rings.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch the threads go on. Change the LAYERS list:
;   each entry is a skip and a color.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * placing points evenly round a circle with SIN and COS
;   * REMAINDER to wrap round from the last nail back to the first
;   * how straight lines can make a curve
;   * the inner circle's radius is R x cos(180 x skip / nails)
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use a skip of 36 (half of 72). What happens and why?
;   * Use 71 nails instead of 72 and a skip of 30.
;   * Draw only every other thread for a lacy look.
; ============================================================

make "nails 72
make "radius 270
make "layers [[33 [200 50 70]] [27 [240 120 40]] [21 [245 200 60]] [15 [60 170 150]] [9 [70 110 210]]]

; Where nail number n is (nails count from 0, starting at the top).
to nail :n
  localmake "angle 360 * :n / :nails
  output list :radius * sin :angle :radius * cos :angle
end

to hammer
  setpencolor [200 200 210] setpensize 6
  penup
  for [n 0 :nails - 1] [dot nail :n]
end

; One layer: from every nail to the nail SKIP places on.
to threads :skip :color
  setpencolor :color setpensize 1
  for [n 0 :nails - 1] [
    penup setpos nail :n
    pendown setpos nail remainder :n + :skip :nails
    wait 1
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [25 25 40]
hammer
foreach :layers [threads first ? last ?]
; hammer again so the nail heads sit on top of the threads
hammer
